  "bf16_partial_hit_interleave": "THIRD MECHANISM, REPRODUCED TWICE (with and without the store clamp): store P -> wait past read-TTL -> request P+S (partial APC hit ~4000, lmcache HIT per server ledger 'Retrieved 800' - the TTL did NOT produce the expected miss) -> fillers -> retrieve P => plausible-but-divergent text, mean |dlp| 0.711/0.713. NOT fixed by the store-side null clamp; the server ledger shows no store-under-miss ever occurred, so this is NOT the F12 store-poisoning path - it lives in the partial-retrieve/interleaving path (candidates: retrieve-side null-page scribble aliasing a live state read; state landing for a mid-sequence chunk under partial vllm_hit).",
  "mp_server_restart": "OPERATIONAL: restarting the MP server under a live engine KILLS the engine (STORE handler: 'No GPU context registered for instance ID', EngineDeadError, kv_load_failure_policy=fail). No reconnect exists."
