  "dominant_defect": "fp8-KV transfer is broken outright on this stack. The served profile uses --kv-cache-dtype fp8, so LMCache could NEVER have produced clean reuse here regardless of #403 and regardless of GDN state - this explains the 2x's 38/38 with divergence 4.4 more directly than state restoration. Root-cause candidates inside the connector: the _SubpagedAttentionViewEdit/fake-view byte arithmetic for 1-byte dtypes, or unregistered fp8 scale surfaces (kv_cache_interface.py:198-207 carve-out).",
  "f12_store_poisoning": "remains source-true (GetStoreMetadata counts APC-hit spans storable, no null filter) but was NOT the operative mechanism in this geometry - the TTL-based miss precondition never materialized (read TTL is not since-write expiry). The ~20-line clamp (receipts/kernel-gap-lmcache-store-clamp.patch) is source-justified hygiene but measured INSUFFICIENT.",
  "recommendation": "DO NOT ENABLE stands, with sharper reasons: (1) fp8-KV transfer must be root-caused/fixed first (blocking, affects every chunk); (2) even at bf16 the partial-hit interleaving corrupts; (3) MP server restart kills the engine. The one positive: the bf16 clean round-trip proves the mamba machinery is sound, so a fix list is finite."
